          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I know if my electrical box is fan-rated?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Take down the canopy and look inside the box. A fan-rated box is normally marked as acceptable for fan support with a maximum weight, and under the electrical code boxes for fans over 35 pounds must state their limit, up to 70 pounds. Plain plastic boxes, boxes marked not for fan support, or boxes held only by drywall need replacing."
          }
