            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Imbalance forces rise sharply with speed, so a small weight or tracking difference that is invisible on low becomes obvious on high. If the mount is solid, wobble that only appears on high is almost always a blade tracking or weight problem. Measure tracking with a yardstick first, then use the balancing clip on each blade."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I balance a ceiling fan without a balancing kit?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. A coin taped to the top of a blade does the same job as a kit weight, using the same trial process: tape it to each blade in turn, find the blade where it helps most, then slide it along to find the best spot. It is heavier than a kit weight, so it is easier to overcorrect. Kits are inexpensive and more precise."
          }
